Step 1: Verify Snort installation
snort -V


Confirm that the Snort version is displayed.
Step 2: Create a detection rule
echo 'alert tcp any any -> any 4444 (msg:"SNORT TEST ALERT"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)' > local.rules


Step 3: Start Snort
For Snort 3, run:
sudo snort -c /etc/snort/snort.lua -R local.rules -i lo -A alert_fast
For Snort 2, run:
sudo snort -c /etc/snort/snort.conf -R local.rules -i lo -A console


Keep Snort running in this terminal.
Step 4: Generate test traffic
Open another terminal and run:
nc -l 4444


Open a third terminal and send test traffic:
echo "Test message" | nc -w 2 127.0.0.1 4444


Step 5: Observe the result
Check the Snort terminal.

Expected output: An alert containing SNORT TEST ALERT.
